	cx 96 lean - - rail-top 4 + cx 96 lean - + rail-top 4 + colour draw-clipped ;

\ === the Lysander's cockpit ===

\ The Lysander's cockpit, laid out from two photographs of Lysanders'
\ instrument panels: one black board across the cockpit, the blind-flying
\ panel's six dials in its middle. To their right the fuel contents' red
\ strip gauge at the top, the priming button, the starter's red button,
\ the boost pump's and the starting magneto's switches and a green lamp,
\ the cylinder temperature's large dial, 100 to 300°C, the Perseus's
\ air-cooled cylinders taking the place of a radiator, the boost gauge in
\ its red rim, the revolution counter numbered 12 to 34 hundred, and along
\ the foot the oil's pressure and temperature and the free air's
\ temperature. To their left the magneto switches, the clock and the
\ brakes' pressure, a row of toggle switches and four banks of four
\ switches. Below the panel the fire extinguisher's red button and the
\ cockpit cooling's white knob, the compass, the throttle and the
\ two-pitch propeller's lever, the tailplane's trim wheel on the left
\ wall, the variable-incidence tailplane the Lysander trimmed by, the
\ pedals and the column's ring grip. The switches, the lamp, the priming
\ button, the fire button and the cooling knob are drawn and do nothing.
\ There is no flaps' lever and no undercarriage's indicator: the slats
\ work the flaps and the wheels are fixed. The cylinder temperature's red
\ mark is at the engine model's limit, an estimate. The photographs'
\ carburettor temperature is left out, the engine model having none.

\ the angle of a cylinder temperature on the photographed dial's scale, 0°C at nine o'clock round over the top to 300°C at three
: cylinder-angle ( celsius -- angle ) 0 300 clamp 300 / 0.5 - PI * ;

\ the cylinder heads' temperature, 0 to 300°C over the top of the dial, numbered 100, 200 and 300 as the photographed dial is, CYL TEMP on its face below them, a red mark at the type's limit
: draw-cylinder-temperature ( cx cy -- )
	| cx cy |
	cx cy medium-radius dial-face
	0 7 1 do k cx cy medium-radius k 50 * cylinder-angle tick loop
	[ 100 200 300 ] ( celsius | cx cy medium-radius celsius cylinder-angle 0.7 celsius "{0:.0f}" format face-text ) each
	plane@type@temperature-limit cylinder-angle to angle
	cx angle sin medium-radius 0.7 * * + cy angle cos medium-radius 0.7 * * -
	cx angle sin medium-radius * + cy angle cos medium-radius * -
	warning-colour draw-segment
	cx cy 8 + "CYL TEMP" dial-ink centred-text
	cx cy medium-radius plane@coolant-temperature cylinder-angle 0.85 needle-colour hand ;

\ the revolution counter as the photographed one: 1,200 to 3,400 a minute on a sweep, numbered in hundreds every 400
: draw-lysander-revolutions ( cx cy -- )
	| cx cy |
	plane@revolutions plane@type@rated-revolutions * to rpm
	cx cy medium-radius rpm 1200 3400 11 [ [ 1200 "12" ] [ 1600 "16" ] [ 2000 "20" ] [ 2400 "24" ] [ 2800 "28" ] [ 3200 "32" ] ] "R.P.M." sweep-dial ;

\ a small dial along the panel's foot, its name on its face and its hand on a sweep, nothing under it
: draw-foot-dial ( cx cy value low high name -- )
	| cx cy value low high name |
	cx cy small-radius dial-face
	cx cy small-radius 4 sweep-ticks
	cx cy 4 + name dial-ink centred-text
	cx cy small-radius value low high sweep 0.85 needle-colour hand ;

\ a bank of four small switches on a plate of their own
: draw-switch-bank ( x top -- )
	| x top |
	x top 64 18 0x050505 fill-span
	x top 64 18 dial-ink 0.6 dimmed outline
	0 4 1 do k
		x 10 + k 15 * + to lever-x
		lever-x top 11 + 2 0x707070 fill-disc
		lever-x 1 - top 3 + 3 7 0xd8d8d0 fill-span
	loop ;

\ a push button with a rim, in a colour, its name under it
: draw-push-button ( cx cy colour name -- )
	| cx cy colour name |
	cx cy 6 dial-ink 0.6 dimmed draw-circle
	cx cy 5 colour fill-disc
	cx cy 9 + name dial-ink centred-text ;

\ the Lysander's cockpit below the windscreen
