\ === the Gladiator's cockpit ===

\ The Gladiator's cockpit, laid out after a photograph of the Shuttleworth
\ Gladiator's panel, with the controls the Historic Aircraft Association's
\ account of flying it and the CAA's airworthiness notes for G-GLAD
\ describe. One grey plate from the panel's top to the floor, its top edge
\ sloping down from the blind panel to the sides with the view showing
\ above the slope, every name on its face (the front view is drawn 44 rows
\ deeper for it, gladiator-view-rows, so the scene runs on behind the
\ slope). The black blind-flying panel in the middle with the six
\ dials in two rows, the column's ring grip over the directional gyro as
\ in the other cockpits. The left board: the oxygen regulator's nameplate
\ and the DELIVERY and SUPPLY labels over its two dials; under them the
\ cylinder temperature's small gauge, lettered ENG as the photograph's
\ (its other lettering unreadable), a riveted plate over the PRESSURE HEAD HEAT
\ label, drawn with a toggle switch on it that the photograph's fittings
\ on that plate do not show, the switch an inference from the label, and
\ the magneto switches' plate at the lower left. The
\ right board: the revolution counter and the boost gauge in its red rim
\ below it (the photograph's OPERATING LIMITS plate between them left
\ out); at its right edge
\ the oil pressure's upright strip gauge in its yellow housing and the
\ oil cooler's cock, a white disc with a red arrow, which every
\ photograph of the type's cockpit shows there (the Swedish J 8's reads
\ KRAN OLJEKYLARE). Under the blind
\ panel a row of three: the fuel contents in a red rim, the pneumatic
\ brakes' triple gauge, the supply needle and one for each wheel, the
\ bicycle lever on the spade grip sending the air to the wheel on the
\ rudder's side, and the oil temperature in an orange rim; the red
\ STARTER button beside them, the Mk II's electric starter. Below them
\ the compass bowl under the column's shaft at the centre; at the left
\ the tailplane trim's indicator dial, the Gladiator's pitch trim being
\ its tailplane's incidence (no rudder bias, none being recorded), and
\ the star-shaped hand wheel that sets it; at the plate's lower left the
\ throttle in its quadrant box, no pitch lever for the fixed-pitch
\ propeller. No flaps' indicator, the photograph having none; no
\ carburettor temperature gauge, as the account has none; the cylinder
\ temperature on the left board's ENG gauge. The account puts the feet on
\ trays below the view, so the Spitfire's frame pedals show only their
\ tops over the foot of the lower slab. The heater's switch and the cooler's
\ cock are drawn and do nothing. The placings follow the photograph,
\ scaled to the view.

\ the Gladiator's plate top, the blind panel's two dial rows, the row of gauges under it, the row along its foot, and its grey
panel-top 4 + constant gladiator-panel-top
\ the rows the Gladiator's front view is drawn in: the plate's top slopes 40 px down from the blind panel to the sides, so the scene runs on behind the slope to the foot of the plate's upper corners
panel-top 44 + constant gladiator-view-rows
panel-top 48 + constant gladiator-upper-row
panel-top 128 + constant gladiator-lower-row
panel-top 194 + constant gladiator-gauge-row
panel-top 202 + constant gladiator-band-row
0x4c4e46 constant gladiator-board-colour

\ the fuel contents gauge in a red rim, FUEL on its face, 0 to the tank's capacity in gallons
: draw-gladiator-fuel ( cx cy -- )
	| cx cy |
	cx cy small-radius plane@fuel 0 plane@fuel-capacity 4 [ [ 0 "0" ] [ plane@fuel-capacity plane@fuel-capacity "{0:.0f}" format ] ] "" sweep-dial
	cx cy 8 - "FUEL" dial-ink centred-text
	cx cy small-radius boost-rim-colour draw-circle
	cx cy small-radius 1 + boost-rim-colour draw-circle ;

\ the boost gauge in its red rim, 32 px in radius, smaller than the revolution counter as the screenshot shows it, BOOST on its face below the centre
: draw-gladiator-boost ( cx cy -- )
	| cx cy |
	32 to radius
	cx cy radius dial-face
	cx cy radius 9 sweep-ticks
	cx cy radius -6 12 [ [ -4 "-4" ] [ 0 "0" ] [ 4 "4" ] [ 8 "8" ] [ 12 "12" ] ] sweep-numerals
	cx cy 20 + "BOOST" dial-ink centred-text
	cx cy radius plane@boost -6 12 sweep 0.85 needle-colour hand
	cx cy radius boost-rim-colour draw-circle
	cx cy radius 1 + boost-rim-colour draw-circle ;

\ a small gauge as the photographed engine gauge: a round bezel whose face is its upper part, the scale an arc of marks across the top with the lowest and highest readings at its ends, the name in the middle, the needle rising from a pivot at the bottom of the bezel over a bar that closes the face
: draw-arc-gauge ( cx cy value low high name -- )
	| cx cy value low high name |
	cx cy 20 dial-face
	cy 12 + to pivot-y
	0 7 1 do k
		k 6 / 1.7 * 0.85 - to angle
		cx angle sin 20 * + pivot-y angle cos 20 * - cx angle sin 24 * + pivot-y angle cos 24 * - dial-ink draw-segment
	loop
	cx 11 - cy 3 - low "{0:.0f}" format 5 dial-ink centred-lettering
	cx 10 + cy 3 - high "{0:.0f}" format 5 dial-ink centred-lettering
	cx cy 3 + name dial-ink centred-text
	cx 16 - cy 10 + cx 16 + cy 10 + dial-ink 0.6 dimmed draw-segment
	cx pivot-y 24 value low high clamp low - high low - / 1.7 * 0.85 - 0.9 needle-colour hand ;

\ the P-type compass in its bowl seen from above and ahead, its card a flat ellipse 24 px across and 9 px high with the lubber line at its far edge and the needle pointing north as the aircraft turns, the bowl's side 10 px below it
: draw-bowl-compass ( cx cy -- )
	| cx cy |
	24 to rx
	9 to ry
	[ 0 25 1 do k cx k PI * 12 / sin rx * + cy k PI * 12 / cos ry * - loop ] to rim
	cx rx - cy rx 2 * 10 grip-colour fill-span
	0 24 1 do k
		rim k 2 * @i to x0
		rim k 2 * 1+ @i to y0
		rim k 2 * 2 + @i to x1
		rim k 2 * 3 + @i to y1
		y0 cy >= y1 cy >= and if
			x0 y0 10 + x1 y1 10 + cx cy 10 + grip-colour fill-face
			x0 y0 10 + x1 y1 10 + grip-edge-colour draw-segment
		then
	loop
	cx rx - cy cx rx - cy 10 + grip-edge-colour draw-segment
	cx rx + cy cx rx + cy 10 + grip-edge-colour draw-segment
	0 24 1 do k
		rim k 2 * @i to x0
		rim k 2 * 1+ @i to y0
		rim k 2 * 2 + @i to x1
		rim k 2 * 3 + @i to y1
		x0 y0 x1 y1 cx cy dial-colour fill-face
		x0 y0 x1 y1 dial-ink draw-segment
	loop
	cx cy ry - cx cy ry - 4 + dial-ink draw-segment
	plane@attitude@forward heading-of negate PI 180 / * to north
	cx cy cx north sin rx 0.8 * * + cy north cos ry 0.8 * * - needle-colour draw-segment
	cx cy cx north sin rx 0.5 * * - cy north cos ry 0.5 * * + dial-ink draw-segment ;

\ the oil cooler's cock, a white disc with a red arrow, as the photographs show it, at open
: draw-cooler-cock ( cx cy -- )
	| cx cy |
	cx cy 20 0xe8e8e0 fill-disc
	cx cy 20 edge-colour draw-circle
	cx 11 + cy 11 + cx 11 - cy 11 - warning-colour draw-segment
	cx 11 - cy 2 - cx 11 - cy 11 - warning-colour draw-segment
	cx 2 - cy 11 - cx 11 - cy 11 - warning-colour draw-segment ;

\ the tailplane trim's indicator as the photographed one: its needle pivoted near the top of the face, hanging down over an arc of marks along the bottom, DN at the arc's left end and UP at its right, TRIM between the pivot and the arc
: draw-trim-dial ( cx cy -- )
	| cx cy |
	cx cy 25 dial-face
	cy 13 - to pivot-y
	0 7 1 do k
		PI k 6 / 1.2 * 0.6 - - to angle
		cx angle sin 26 * + pivot-y angle cos 26 * - cx angle sin 30 * + pivot-y angle cos 30 * - dial-ink draw-segment
	loop
	cx 13 - cy 1 + "DN" dial-ink centred-text
	cx 13 + cy 1 + "UP" dial-ink centred-text
	cx cy 8 - "TRIM" dial-ink centred-text
	cx pivot-y 30 PI plane@trim -1 1 clamp 0.6 * - 0.85 needle-colour hand ;

\ a black label plate with its wording across it
: draw-label ( cx top width text -- )
	| cx top width text |
	cx width 2 / - top width 11 0x050505 fill-span
	cx width 2 / - top width 11 dial-ink 0.6 dimmed outline
	cx top 2 + text dial-ink centred-text ;

\ the oxygen regulator as the Gladiator's plate carries it: OXYGEN REGULATOR engraved across the top, DELIVERY and SUPPLY under it, the two dials close together below them with a bracket between, the delivery's set for the height above 10,000 ft and the supply's full with the lower left of its face red, as the Hurricane's
: draw-gladiator-oxygen ( cx cy -- )
	| cx cy |
	cx cy 48 - "OXYGEN REGULATOR" dial-ink centred-text
	cx 27 - cy 36 - "DELIVERY" dial-ink centred-text
	cx 27 + cy 36 - "SUPPLY" dial-ink centred-text
	cx cy 22 - cx cy 22 + edge-colour draw-segment
	plane@position second 3.28084 * 1000 / to thousands
	thousands 10 < if 0 else thousands then to delivery
	cx 27 - cy medium-radius delivery 0 40 8 [ [ 0 "0" ] [ 20 "20" ] [ 40 "40" ] ] "" sweep-dial
	cx 27 + to supply-x
	supply-x cy medium-radius dial-face
	0 17 1 do k
		k 0.1 * 1.9 - to angle
		supply-x angle sin medium-radius 0.35 * * + cy angle cos medium-radius 0.35 * * -
		supply-x angle sin medium-radius 0.9 * * + cy angle cos medium-radius 0.9 * * -
		warning-colour 0.7 dimmed draw-segment
	loop
	supply-x cy medium-radius 4 sweep-ticks
	supply-x cy medium-radius 1 0 1 sweep 0.85 needle-colour hand ;

\ the revolution counter as the Lysander's, 1,200 to 3,400 a minute numbered in hundreds, at the large size with R.P.M. on its face below the centre
: draw-gladiator-revolutions ( cx cy -- )
	| cx cy |
	plane@revolutions plane@type@rated-revolutions * to rpm
	cx cy large-radius rpm 1200 3400 11 [ [ 1200 "12" ] [ 1600 "16" ] [ 2000 "20" ] [ 2400 "24" ] [ 2800 "28" ] [ 3200 "32" ] ] "" sweep-dial
	cx cy 22 + "R.P.M." dial-ink centred-text ;

\ the brakes' twin-needle gauge, its name on its face above the needles: the supply needle on the sweep, and from the bottom a needle for each wheel, swung out by the air the lever sends it, all of it to the wheel on the rudder's side and both with the bar centred
: draw-brake-gauge ( cx cy -- )
	| cx cy |
	cx cy small-radius dial-face
	cx cy small-radius 6 sweep-ticks
	cx cy small-radius 200 0 300 sweep 0.85 dial-ink hand
	controls@brakes if 1 else 0 then to squeezed
	[ -1 1 ] ( side |
		squeezed 1 controls@yaw side * + 0 1 clamp * to share
		cx cy small-radius PI side 0.4 share 0.6 * + * - 0.7 needle-colour hand
	) each
	cx cy 9 - "BRAKES" dial-ink centred-text ;

\ the trim's hand wheel, a six-pointed star, its points 26 px out, each pair of points joined by one concave arc that passes 18 px from the centre midway between them: the circle through the two points and that midpoint has its centre 38.96 px out along the bisector and a radius of 20.96 px, and the arc runs round its inner side; filled in gunmetal and turned with its setting
0x6e7074 constant gunmetal-colour
: draw-star-wheel ( cx cy setting -- )
	| cx cy setting |
	6 iota ( k |
		setting 15 * k PI * 3 / + PI 6 / + to bisector
		9 iota ( t |
			3.810 t 0.1671 * - to arc-angle
			38.96 arc-angle cos 20.96 * + to out
			arc-angle sin 20.96 * to across
			[ cx bisector sin out * + bisector cos across * + cy bisector cos out * - bisector sin across * + ]
		) map
	) map [ ] ' concat reduce to outline
	outline size to n-points
	0 n-points 1 do k
		outline k @i spread to y0 to x0
		outline k 1+ n-points mod @i spread to y1 to x1
		x0 y0 x1 y1 cx cy gunmetal-colour fill-face
		x0 y0 x1 y1 grip-edge-colour draw-segment
	loop ;

\ the throttle quadrant on the left wall under the magneto plate, seen side-on from the seat as a photograph of a Gladiator's shows it: a light metal housing with two slots up it and two levers with black ball knobs, their rods rising from below the screen's edge, the throttle's knob travelling up its slot as the throttle opens and the mixture's up the other as it goes richer (the photograph's second lever, taken for the mixture's); no pitch lever, the propeller fixed-pitch, and no cut-out, the Mercury's rated boost its most
0xb4b4ac constant quadrant-colour
: draw-gladiator-throttle ( -- )
	6 panel-top 178 + 36 50 quadrant-colour fill-span
	6 panel-top 178 + 36 50 grip-edge-colour outline
	[ [ 16 plane@throttle ] [ 30 plane@mixture ] ] ( lever |
		lever spread to setting to x
		x panel-top 184 + x panel-top 222 + grip-colour draw-segment
		panel-top 220 + setting 34 * - to knob-y
		-1 2 1 do k x k + screen-height x k + knob-y grip-colour draw-segment loop
		x knob-y 5 0x101010 fill-disc
		x knob-y 5 grip-edge-colour draw-circle
		x 2 - knob-y 2 - 1 0xd8d8d0 fill-disc
	) each ;

\ the Gladiator's cockpit below the windscreen
: draw-gladiator-panel ( -- )
	0 gladiator-view-rows view-width screen-height gladiator-view-rows - wall-colour fill-span
	24 panel-top 44 + 592 screen-height panel-top - 44 - gladiator-board-colour fill-span
	194 gladiator-panel-top 252 40 gladiator-board-colour fill-span
	24 panel-top 44 + 194 gladiator-panel-top 194 panel-top 44 + gladiator-board-colour fill-face
	446 gladiator-panel-top 616 panel-top 44 + 446 panel-top 44 + gladiator-board-colour fill-face
	24 panel-top 44 + 194 gladiator-panel-top edge-colour draw-segment
	194 gladiator-panel-top 446 gladiator-panel-top edge-colour draw-segment
	446 gladiator-panel-top 616 panel-top 44 + edge-colour draw-segment
	24 panel-top 44 + 24 screen-height edge-colour draw-segment
	616 panel-top 44 + 616 screen-height edge-colour draw-segment
	190 panel-top 12 + 190 panel-top 172 + edge-colour draw-segment
	450 panel-top 12 + 450 panel-top 172 + edge-colour draw-segment
	194 panel-top 8 + 252 160 blind-panel-colour fill-span
	194 panel-top 8 + 252 160 edge-colour outline
	236 gladiator-upper-row draw-airspeed
	320 gladiator-upper-row draw-horizon
	404 gladiator-upper-row draw-climb
	236 gladiator-lower-row draw-altimeter
	320 gladiator-lower-row draw-gyro
	404 gladiator-lower-row draw-turn-and-slip
	40 panel-top 44 + 146 68 blind-panel-colour fill-span
	40 panel-top 44 + 186 panel-top 18 + 186 panel-top 44 + blind-panel-colour fill-face
	70 panel-top 112 + 116 28 blind-panel-colour fill-span
	70 panel-top 140 + 84 32 blind-panel-colour fill-span
	154 panel-top 140 + 186 panel-top 140 + 154 panel-top 172 + blind-panel-colour fill-face
	[ [ 40 44 ] [ 186 18 ] [ 186 140 ] [ 154 172 ] [ 70 172 ] [ 70 112 ] [ 40 112 ] ] to slab
	0 slab size 1 do k
		slab k @i spread panel-top + slab k 1+ slab size mod @i spread panel-top + edge-colour draw-segment
	loop
	111 panel-top 88 + draw-gladiator-oxygen
	98 panel-top 142 + plane@coolant-temperature 0 300 "ENG" draw-arc-gauge
	36 panel-top 116 + 32 56 blind-panel-colour fill-span
	36 panel-top 116 + 32 56 edge-colour outline
	52 panel-top 120 + "MAG." dial-ink centred-text
	52 panel-top 166 + draw-magnetos
	130 panel-top 116 + 32 30 0x141412 fill-span
	130 panel-top 116 + 32 30 edge-colour outline
	[ [ 133 119 ] [ 159 119 ] [ 133 143 ] [ 159 143 ] ] ( rivet | rivet spread panel-top + 1 grip-edge-colour fill-disc ) each
	146 panel-top 142 + draw-toggle
	121 panel-top 150 + 38 16 0x141412 fill-span
	120 panel-top 151 + 40 14 0x141412 fill-span
	120 panel-top 150 + 40 16 edge-colour outline
	140 panel-top 151 + "PRESSURE" 5 dial-ink centred-lettering
	140 panel-top 158 + "HEAD HEAT" 5 dial-ink centred-lettering
	454 panel-top 44 + 146 96 blind-panel-colour fill-span
	454 panel-top 18 + 600 panel-top 44 + 454 panel-top 44 + blind-panel-colour fill-face
	486 panel-top 140 + 114 32 blind-panel-colour fill-span
	454 panel-top 140 + 486 panel-top 140 + 486 panel-top 172 + blind-panel-colour fill-face
	[ [ 454 18 ] [ 600 44 ] [ 600 172 ] [ 486 172 ] [ 454 140 ] ] to slab
	0 slab size 1 do k
		slab k @i spread panel-top + slab k 1+ slab size mod @i spread panel-top + edge-colour draw-segment
	loop
	497 panel-top 64 + draw-gladiator-revolutions
	503 panel-top 138 + draw-gladiator-boost
	562 panel-top 54 + "OIL" dial-ink centred-text
	562 panel-top 62 + 18 40 plane@oil-pressure 120 / 0xd8b830 "" draw-strip-gauge
	570 panel-top 144 + draw-cooler-cock
	60 panel-top 176 + 520 34 blind-panel-colour fill-span
	[ 0 53 1 do k 60 k 10 * + dup 180 460 clamp 180 - 280 / PI * sin 18 * negate panel-top 228 + + loop ] to arc
	0 52 1 do k
		arc k 2 * @i to x0
		arc k 2 * 1+ @i to y0
		arc k 2 * 2 + @i to x1
		arc k 2 * 3 + @i to y1
		x0 panel-top 210 + x1 panel-top 210 + x1 y1 blind-panel-colour fill-face
		x0 panel-top 210 + x1 y1 x0 y0 blind-panel-colour fill-face
		x0 y0 x1 y1 edge-colour draw-segment
